## What is this?

Collections agents waste a lot of time waiting for calls to connect. There are two ways to fix that:

| Mode | Idea | Trade-off |
|---|---|---|
| **Progressive** | 1 free agent → 1 outbound call | Safe and predictable, but agents can sit idle |
| **Predictive** | Dial *more* numbers than you have agents for, betting on the answer rate | Better utilization, but risks a borrower answering with nobody there to talk to them (an **abandoned call** — a real compliance problem, not just bad UX) |

This project builds both modes, with one non-negotiable rule sitting between them and the phone system: **a Safety Controller that pacing logic can never bypass, no matter how confident its prediction is.**

---

